<title>MEXICO: Mexico crude port Pajaritos shut again amid winds.</title>
<headline>Mexico crude port Pajaritos shut again amid winds.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's third largest crude port Pajaritos in Veracruz state was shut at 1400 local/2000 GMT Monday as wind speeds escalated, a port official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The port was shut over the weekend and reopened at 0800 local/1400 GMT Monday as winds calmed. About 399,000 barrels per day (bpd) of crude are shipped from the terminal, according to the latest figures from state oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex).</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
